ender-0, render-1 and render-2 the leaflets are narrow, linear and sharp-tipped, giving the fronds a bristly edge. In render-2 they sit at somewhat varied angles. The V-section/plumose insertion is not clearly resolvable.", "The trunk carries no foliage, branches or epiphytes. The only features are a few small dark stub-like nubs spaced sparsely along it.", "render-3 is marked visibility 'hidden' in the metadata, but the supplied image clearly shows the trunk surface. It matches render-2 (visibility 'shown').", "There is no dead-frond skirt (secondary) and no crownshaft (consistent with crown-shaft-absent). Trunk colour is a flat dark brown and does not show the grey/reddish weathering in the references (secondary).", "The render's finish is clean and consistent, and at least as coherent as the spruce anchor (anchor-0). Finish quality is not the limiting factor."], "findings": [{"observation": "Both seeds show a single apical rosette of arching pinnate fronds, with the lowest fronds drooping below the crown base. The crown reads as a palm's, as reference-0 and reference-1 do.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The render crown has fewer fronds (about 15-20) than the inventory's 30-60, and the fronds are narrower and less full than in reference-0. The rosette identity still reads. Fuller, longer fronds would be a refinement, not a missing defining trait.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Frond count and leaflet length/width may still sit at conservative values, but no specific mechanism is established."}, {"observation": "The trunk is straight with near-constant diameter in both seeds. The strong lean and S-curve in reference-0 is inventory variation, and the owner wants a straight trunk.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Nothing grows on the trunk in either seed: no foliage, branches or epiphytes. The ferns in reference-1 and reference-2 are variation, not a requirement.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-1"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "The trunk surface is smooth with only a few sparse nubs. The spiral lattice of retained leaf bases in reference-1 and reference-2 is missing.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The inventory states that retained leaf bases are not yet expressed by the generator. The few nubs may be sparse output from the trunk organs (fn-110), but this is not established."}, {"observation": "The trunk has no fibrous matting between leaf bases.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "There are no pendent fruit clusters below the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "The owner's note says the date cluster (fn-111) has not landed."}, {"observation": "render-3 is flagged visibility 'hidden', yet its content matches the 'shown' render-2 trunk surface. This leaves some ambiguity about what the P-BASE view was meant to show.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "render-2"], "impact": "variation", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "An apical rosette of pinnate fronds: the upper fronds rise and the older ones recurve and droop. The crown is sparser than in the references, which is a refinement, not a defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The leaflets are narrow and sharp-pointed with a bristly frond margin, and they sit at somewhat varied angles in render-2. Fine grouped/V-section insertion cannot be resolved at this scale."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The render trunk is a smooth cylinder with a few isolated nubs. There is no spiral lattice of blunt wedge stubs, which is the defining character in the references."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The render shows no fibre or husk. The trunk surface is uniform and smooth."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "One unbranched columnar stem of near-constant diameter carries the crown in both seeds."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "No fruit bunches appear in either seed. Reference-0 shows orange pendent bunches. The owner's note says fn-111 has not landed; that explains the absence but does not resolve it."}, {"trait_id": "owner-fronds-long-arching", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "The fronds are long enough for the crown to read as an arching palm rosette with drooping lower fronds, and the crown-to-height proportion is close to reference-0. Fuller leaflets and more fronds remain optional refinement."}, {"trait_id": "owner-trunk-straight-constant", "status": "pass", "evidence_